WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.166
For AABW P5, team memory dies in
private chats and local workflows,

2
00:00:05.283 --> 00:00:07.732
so a handoff can fail when people move on.

3
00:00:07.906 --> 00:00:12.098
Organizational AI Memory turns that
know-how into reviewed, versioned,

4
00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:16.568
cited capability that authorized people
and agents can find at task start,

5
00:00:16.603 --> 00:00:18.367
without exposing private memory.

6
00:00:18.693 --> 00:00:22.210
A delivery lead asks: prepare
a website delivery handoff.

7
00:00:22.535 --> 00:00:26.959
Before any generation, deterministic
PostgreSQL retrieval selects three

8
00:00:26.994 --> 00:00:30.314
approved records: a brief
prompt, a delivery workflow,

9
00:00:30.349 --> 00:00:32.311
and the source-first decision pattern.

10
00:00:32.404 --> 00:00:36.061
The screen shows their versions,
review state, why each worked,

11
00:00:36.107 --> 00:00:37.338
and source evidence.

12
00:00:37.454 --> 00:00:41.807
The organization retains typed, versioned,
reviewed capability with explicit

13
00:00:41.877 --> 00:00:46.777
provenance from asset to observation to
source turn, not just a static prompt.

14
00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.900
Codex Spark can adapt
only the selected records.

15
00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:52.628
Citations are validated against that set.

16
00:00:52.686 --> 00:00:57.214
In this fresh recording Spark produced
a six-step adaptation grounded in those

17
00:00:57.261 --> 00:01:01.185
same three records. Deterministic
selection remained authoritative.

18
00:01:01.231 --> 00:01:04.935
The model can adapt the plan; it
cannot decide what the company knows.

19
00:01:05.005 --> 00:01:08.442
Personal memory is the private
support lane for this P5 system,

20
00:01:08.511 --> 00:01:09.649
not a second product.

21
00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:14.107
Synthetic employee Mai Nguyen records
an owner-only lesson with context,

22
00:01:14.154 --> 00:01:15.721
evidence, and why it worked.

23
00:01:15.837 --> 00:01:19.169
Saving it does not publish it
and does not grant agent access.

24
00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:22.200
Before consent, retrieval
returns no grounded match.

25
00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:24.452
She explicitly shares
the current revision.

26
00:01:24.522 --> 00:01:30.396
The employee preview then shows the
memory ID, revision, SHA-256 citation,

27
00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.670
and audit receipt. That preview
is not physical execution.

28
00:01:33.728 --> 00:01:37.826
The linked Personal Memory Agent runs
under a dedicated locked Linux identity

29
00:01:37.908 --> 00:01:39.394
and retrieves through a broker.

30
00:01:39.463 --> 00:01:43.039
Protected source, model
credentials, outbound IP sockets,

31
00:01:43.062 --> 00:01:45.524
and direct PostgreSQL remain denied.

32
00:01:45.547 --> 00:01:49.157
When Mai edits the lesson, the new
revision returns to owner-only.

33
00:01:49.204 --> 00:01:53.453
Retrieval fails closed until she
re-consents, exposing only the new

34
00:01:53.523 --> 00:01:54.684
revision and hash.

35
00:01:54.753 --> 00:01:58.271
Separately quarantined organizational
input may become a candidate.

36
00:01:58.294 --> 00:02:01.789
An independent reviewer can approve
it; the architect can promote only a

37
00:02:01.848 --> 00:02:05.272
governed draft, while direct
canonical writes remain denied.

38
00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:09.684
Synthetic pack inventory shows
nine assets, five task definitions,

39
00:02:09.731 --> 00:02:14.340
thirteen deterministic task-to-asset
mappings, and three authored gap signals.

40
00:02:14.514 --> 00:02:19.320
These are inventory signals only, not
return on investment or trend analysis.

41
00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:24.069
The deployed release passed
275 API and security tests,

42
00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:28.225
twenty-two build-bound identity
controls, thirty-five browser checks,

43
00:02:28.307 --> 00:02:30.687
and seven physical-agent boundary checks.

44
00:02:31.012 --> 00:02:35.853
Five isolated real-PostgreSQL integration
cases remain recorded contract

45
00:02:35.911 --> 00:02:38.721
evidence rather than a
fresh live-database run.

46
00:02:39.162 --> 00:02:43.167
A proposed enterprise pilot would
measure reuse, recommendation acceptance,

47
00:02:43.237 --> 00:02:48.287
review turnaround, gaps, and access
denial; no user pilot or testimonial is

48
00:02:48.357 --> 00:02:48.844
claimed.

49
00:02:48.903 --> 00:02:52.351
When people move on, the organization
keeps reviewed capability,

50
00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:54.406
not their identity or private memory.
